  "implementation": [
    "Safe forbidunsafe RenderedMessage owns String before WorkspaceReservation. Original WeakOwner/RuntimeAccess required, reservation before physical copy, capacity reconciled before publication, data destroyed before original ticket.",
    "Cache admission happens before publishing buffer/cache state, so cap1 denial preserves previous raw buffer and previous exact original charge and restores error flags.",
    "ErrorState owns admitted cache; equality compares borrowed str directly, and old cache destruction occurs after state lend ends.",
    "Seven direct cache tests cover exact retained charge, replacement/clearing, immutable source copy, panic, cap1, inactive/revoked owner and foreign allocated/workspace counters.",
    "Existing default/canonical boundary tests assert the exact intentional persistent cache charge, then clear and require zero; original source liveness, tags, GC gap1/wait1, flags and no foreign mutations remain asserted."
